---
layout: layouts/base.njk
description: A practical field guide to digital privacy and operational security. Threat modeling, hardening guides, tool recommendations, and lessons from real OPSEC failures.
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<div class="home">
  <div class="home__intro">
    <div class="home__intro-text">
      <h1>The Privacy Cookbook</h1>
      <p class="home__tagline">{{ site.tagline }}</p>
      <p>
        Recipes, not sermons. Every guide here starts from a threat model,
        explains the tradeoffs, and tells you what to actually do. Written and
        reviewed in the open; no ads, no analytics, no affiliate links.
      </p>
      <div class="home__actions">
        <a class="button button--primary" href="/start-here/">Start here</a>
        <a class="button button--secondary" href="/recommendations/">Recommendations</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <img class="home__mark" src="/assets/img/pigeon.png" alt="The Privacy Cookbook mark: a pigeon with a surveillance camera for a head" width="130" height="140">
  </div>

  <h2>Browse the cookbook</h2>
  <ul class="home__sections">
    {% for section in nav %}
    {% set sectionPage = collections.all | pageByUrl(section.url) %}
    <li>
      <a href="{{ section.url }}">
        <span class="home__section-title">{{ section.title }}</span>
        {% if sectionPage and sectionPage.data.description %}
        <span class="home__section-desc">{{ sectionPage.data.description }}</span>
        {% endif %}
      </a>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <h2>How to use this site</h2>
  <p>
    If you are new, read <a href="/start-here/threat-modeling/">Threat Modeling</a> first.
    Privacy advice without a threat model is just a shopping list. Once you know
    what you are protecting and from whom, the rest of the cookbook tells you
    which measures are worth your time and which are not.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <a href="/darwin-awards/">Darwin Awards</a> section documents real,
    publicly reported operational security failures — not to celebrate arrests,
    but because a mistake that unmasked someone with everything to lose is a
    mistake worth understanding.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site is not</h2>
  <p>
    This is not a product catalog and not a promise of anonymity. No tool makes
    you anonymous; some tools reduce specific exposures under specific
    conditions, and every recommendation here says which. Where we are unsure,
    we say so.
  </p>
</div>
